    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into the June 6 slate prioritizing high-ceiling matchups against soft pitching, headlined by our outfield tandem of **Kyle Tucker** (78.74) and **Andy Pages** (70.49). Both benefit significantly from a favorable clash against Jack Kochanowicz, whose high xERA (5.12) provides the cleanest path to multi-hit and multi-RBI potential. **Gunnar Henderson** (64.41) remains a core start; despite facing a tougher arm in Fisher, his 85% stolen base frequency against slow-delivery pitchers makes him a premium play in our scarcest category. Meanwhile, **Sam Antonacci** (63.14) is poised for a breakout performance at the top of the order against Painter, with wind conditions and favorable xwOBA projections amplifying his scoring floor.\n\nOur bench logic was most tested by the decision to keep **Brayan Rocchio** (43.55) out of the active lineup. While he cleared our \"Below Floor\" threshold, he was ultimately surpassed by **Nasim Nunez** (60.43) and **Miguel Vargas** (61.55), who boast stronger lineup placement and superior platoon splits for today's specific pitching profiles. We are monitoring **Jackson Merrill**, **Andy Pages**, and **Kyle Tucker** closely, as their scores are currently based on projected lineups; any shift lower in the batting order could trigger a recalibration of their daily efficiency. While we are comfortable with our active roster, **Coby Mayo** (38.80) fell just short of the 40.0 baseline, reinforcing our commitment to maximizing every plate appearance to secure the edge in 5x5 categories.",
